<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paul Gauguin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1848–1903</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Paul Gauguin was a French Post-Impressionist painter, sculptor and printmaker. Leaving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> in 1891, he spent most of his remaining years in Tahiti and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marquesas-islands">Marquesas Islands</a>, where he painted the works, bold in colour and simplified in form, that shaped European images of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polynesia">Polynesia</a>. He died at Atuona on Hiva Oa, and his work influenced modern artists from the Fauves to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pablo-picasso">Picasso</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paul-gauguin.jpg" alt="Paul Gauguin" width="320" height="406" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Louis-Maurice Boutet de Monvel · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Paul_Gauguin_1891.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
